senses.gloss:
उप-√ चर् P. -चरति, to go towards, come near, approach, RV. vii, 46, 2; TS. v, 7, 6, 1; ŚBr.; R.;
to come near, wait upon, serve, attend, assist, bear a hand, ŚBr.; MBh.; Mṛcch.; Daś. &c.;
to approach, set about, undertake, perform, TS. iii, 1, 6, 1; ŚBr.;
to attend on (a patient), physic (a person), treat, tend, nurse, Suśr.; Pañcat.;
to use figuratively or metaphorically, apply figuratively (generally Pass. -चर्यते), VarBṛS.; Sāh.; Sarvad. &c.

उपा-√ चर् P. -चरति, to come near to, approach, RV. i, 46, 14; 187, 3; ŚBr. ii, iv;
to attend upon, wait on, serve, be obedient, RV.; MBh. ii, 408;
to physic, Suśr.

उप-√ 1. चि P. -चिनोति, to gather together, TS. i, 1, 7, 2;
to heap up, collect, hoard up, accumulate;
to increase, strengthen, MBh.; Kum.; Suśr.; Megh. &c.;
to pour over, cover, overload:
Pass. -चीयते, to be heaped together or accumulated;
to increase, become strong, MBh.; Suśr.; Rājat.; Hit. &c.;
to gain advantage, succeed, be prosperous, Mn. viii, 169;
to be covered with;
to cover one's self, furnish one's self with, MBh.; Suśr.

उप-च्छन्द् (उप-√ छन्द्), Caus. -च्छन्दयति, to conciliate (privately by flattering or coaxing language), coax, entice;
to seduce, Prab.; Rājat.; Kathās.;
to supplicate, beg, Ragh. v, 58.
